<title>JAPAN: Sega, Bandai shares wilt due to unclear future.</title>
<headline>Sega, Bandai shares wilt due to unclear future.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of video game giant Sega Enterprises Ltd and toymaker Bandai Co Ltd fell on Monday afternoon, hit by uncertainties over the future of the two firms after they merge, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 0445 GMT, Sega was down 200 yen at 3,120 yen. Bandai had shed 150 yen to 2,270 yen.  </p>
<p>Brokers said investors were still trying to decide whether the merger, due to takeplace in October, was a &quot;buy&quot;or a &quot;sell&quot; situation, as views were mixed.</p>
<p>&quot;We get the impression that this is a case of two firms that both face hard times deciding to team up,&quot; a broker at a second-tier brokerage said.</p>
</text>
